{
  "$comment": "Known-good reference: AngeloJacobo/UberDDR3 as simulated by its own testbench (ddr3_dimm_micron_sim.sv, TWO_LANES_x8, den8192Mb sg125, CONTROLLER_CLK_PERIOD 12ns, DDR3_CLK_PERIOD 3ns, SPEED_BIN 3). Compiled from the DDR3-800/8Gb/x16/2-lane choices, then overridden to UberDDR3's real clocking (12ns/3ns, CL=CWL=5) and its SPEED_BIN=3 ns table. tRRD/tFAW are NOT enforced by UberDDR3 (no occurrence in ddr3_controller.v); the values here are the JEDEC/Micron sg125 x16 minimums (tRRD max(4nCK,7.5ns), tFAW 40ns) so the assertions state what the DRAM requires, not what the controller promises.",
